# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THIS REPOSITORY IS PUBLIC. Everything below exists so that a careless
# `git add -A` cannot publish credentials or customer data. Rules are scoped to
# the repo root with a leading slash, so tracked assets under attached_assets/
# and client/ are unaffected. To commit something these rules cover, name the
# file explicitly and check it first -- do not relax the pattern.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Secrets. outreach-runner/.env carries live SES keys.
.env
.env.*
**/.env

# Customer data: real names, emails and phone numbers. The lead lists at the
# repo root hold roughly 9,000 people between them.
/*.csv
/*_leads.json
/badge_leads*.json
/call_sheet_*.md
/gbp_review_replies.md

# One-off ops scripts kept at the repo root. 382 of the 468 present on 2026-08-28
# carry hardcoded live credentials (root SSH, DB, SES), so none may be committed.
# They are deliberately NOT moved out of the tree: quantum-sync-status.ps1 hashes
# C:\quantum\*.cjs against /opt/quantum-ops on the CRM VPS, and relocating them
# would break that check. Scripts already tracked here stay tracked -- these rules
# only stop new ones being added. To commit a genuinely clean script, `git add -f`
# it after confirming it reads every secret from the environment.
/*.cjs
/*.py
/*.js
/*.mjs
/*.sh
/*.php
/*.bat

# Local scratch: RLI portal screenshots, diagnostic dumps, run logs.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
/*.png
/*.log
/*.zip
/*.b64
